### Lot 5 step 4a demo, accreditations and invitations (IntelliJ HTTP client): plan lot-5 §12.1 Exit 4a (1)-(7) on one
### instance; Lot5InvitationsFlowTest runs the same flow in CI.
#
# Start the backend with the dev profile on port 8080 (dev seed: ATLAS FC, Admin Dev +212600000001, Ops Dev
# +212600000003, Finance Dev +212600000004, Grand Stade with Nord, Est, Honneur, Sud and gates P1-P7, P1 serving
# Honneur; the manifest job runs every minute; WhatsApp goes to the log):
#   docker compose up -d && SERVER_PORT=8080 GATE_MANIFEST_LEAD=2400h SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./gradlew bootRun
# GATE_MANIFEST_LEAD: a scanner gets an event's manifest only from starts_at minus this lead (default 3h). The demo
# match is in January 2027, so 2400h (100 days) lets the scanner load it today (step 4); it changes nothing else.
# Every phone logs in with the dev OTP 123456 (JOMHOR_DEV_FIXED_OTP, dev default). The press phones are made up.
#
# Step 1.4 creates the zone PRESSE once: on a re-run it answers 409/422 and 1.3 has already found it. 1.5 makes P1 serve
# Honneur and PRESSE (P2-P7 don't: a press QR there scans MAUVAISE ZONE). Each run makes a new match, so the quotas
# start afresh. At the end, backend/loadtest/check.sql must print no rows:
#   docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U jomhor -d jomhor < loadtest/check.sql

@base = http://localhost:8080/v1
@org = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@venue = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000301
@p1 = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000401
@adminPhone = +212600000001
@opsPhone = +212600000003
@financePhone = +212600000004
@nadiaPhone = +212611155001
@salmaPhone = +212611155002
@code = 123456

### ---------- (0) logins ----------

### 0.1 OPS (Ops Dev): ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}"}

### 0.2 OPS: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("orgToken", response.body.token); %}

### 0.3 ADMIN (Admin Dev): ask for a code (revoke, step 6)
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}"}

### 0.4 ADMIN: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.token); %}

### ---------- (1) B10 + B2: PRESSE (60) served by P1; "Presse" and "Invités" (Accès: Invitations) ----------

### 1.1 OPS: the Grand Stade zones (Honneur, and PRESSE from an earlier run)
GET {{base}}/org/venues/{{venue}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

> {% client.global.set("honneurId", response.body.zones.find(z => z.code === "HONNEUR").id);
     const presse = response.body.zones.find(z => z.code === "PRESSE");
     if (presse) client.global.set("presseId", presse.id); %}

### 1.2 OPS: zone PRESSE, capacity 60 -> 201 (first run only)
POST {{base}}/org/venues/{{venue}}/zones
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "PRESSE", "name": "Tribune de presse", "capacity": 60, "seated": true}

> {% if (response.status === 201) client.global.set("presseId", response.body.id); %}

### 1.3 OPS: P1 serves Honneur and PRESSE -> 200
PUT {{base}}/org/gates/{{p1}}/zones
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_ids": [{{honneurId}}, {{presseId}}]}

### 1.4 OPS: the match (DRAFT)
POST {{base}}/org/events
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"venue_id": "{{venue}}", "event_type": "FOOTBALL_MATCH", "title": "ATLAS FC – Démo invitations",
 "starts_at": "2027-01-17T19:00:00Z", "metadata": {"opponent": "Démo"}}

> {% client.global.set("match", response.body.id); %}

### 1.5 OPS: "Presse" in PRESSE (Invitations, 0 DH, quota 40)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{presseId}}, "name": "Presse", "price_mad": 0, "quota": 40, "audience": "INVITE"}

> {% client.global.set("presseCat", response.body.id); %}

### 1.6 OPS: "Invités" in Honneur (Invitations, quota 50)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{honneurId}}, "name": "Invités", "price_mad": 0, "quota": 50, "audience": "INVITE"}

> {% client.global.set("invitesCat", response.body.id); %}

### 1.7 OPS: an INVITE price at 50 DH -> 422 VALIDATION_FAILED, reason INVITE_PRICE
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{honneurId}}, "name": "Invités payants", "price_mad": 5000, "quota": 5, "audience": "INVITE"}

### 1.8 OPS: "Plein tarif" in Honneur (ALL, 300 DH), so fans have something to buy
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{honneurId}}, "name": "Plein tarif", "price_mad": 30000, "quota": 100}

### 1.9 OPS: publish (DRAFT -> ON_SALE)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (2) B7: issue ----------

### 2.1 OPS: 3 press accreditations, two on WhatsApp, one on paper -> 201 {status PAID, channel POS, total_mad 0}
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"invitation_id": "{{$random.uuid}}", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{presseCat}}", "qty": 3, "holders": [
  {"name": "Nadia Berrada", "phone": "{{nadiaPhone}}"},
  {"name": "Salma Tazi", "phone": "{{salmaPhone}}"},
  {"name": "Karim El Idrissi"}]}]}

> {% client.global.set("pressId", response.body.id); %}

# 2.2 Idempotency: re-send 2.1 with "invitation_id": "{{pressId}}" -> 200, the same order, nothing new.

### 2.3 OPS: 10 "Invités" for a partner, one name, no phone -> 201
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"invitation_id": "{{$random.uuid}}", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{invitesCat}}", "qty": 10, "holders": [
  {"name": "Atlas Assurances"}, {"name": "Atlas Assurances"}, {"name": "Atlas Assurances"},
  {"name": "Atlas Assurances"}, {"name": "Atlas Assurances"}, {"name": "Atlas Assurances"},
  {"name": "Atlas Assurances"}, {"name": "Atlas Assurances"}, {"name": "Atlas Assurances"},
  {"name": "Atlas Assurances"}]}]}

> {% client.global.set("partnerId", response.body.id); %}

### 2.4 OPS: B7 batches -> newest first; press tickets WHATSAPP, WHATSAPP, PAPER; partner tickets all PAPER; no phone
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 2.5 OPS: "Imprimer" the partner slips -> 10 tickets with qr, category {name: "Invités"}, Cache-Control no-store
GET {{base}}/org/invitations/{{partnerId}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 2.6 OPS: print the press batch -> 3 slips with qr, category "Presse" (Karim's is the paper one)
GET {{base}}/org/invitations/{{pressId}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

> {% client.global.set("karimTicket", response.body.tickets.find(t => t.holder_label === "Karim I.").id); %}

### ---------- (3) Delivery ----------

### 3.1 Nadia (journalist): code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{nadiaPhone}}"}

### 3.2 Nadia: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{nadiaPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("nadiaToken", response.body.token); %}

### 3.3 Nadia's Billets -> the press ticket in PRESSE with k_t. Salma downloads her PDF on W5 the same way. The backend
### log shows both WhatsApp deliveries (simulated provider).
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{nadiaToken}}

### ---------- (4) Gate (offline scanner, by hand) ----------
# Assign a scanner to P1 in B6 for this match. Nadia's QR at P1 -> VALIDÉ; at P3 -> MAUVAISE ZONE. A printed partner
# slip at P1 -> VALIDÉ once, then DÉJÀ ENTRÉ. After the sync, B5 shows PRESSE entered 1.

### 4.1 B5: reconciliation -> zones PRESSE {sold 3, entered 1 after Nadia's scan}
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (5) Quota ----------

### 5.1 OPS: 38 more press places would make 41 -> 409 SOLD_OUT ("Plus de places Presse"), nothing written
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"invitation_id": "{{$random.uuid}}", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{presseCat}}", "qty": 38, "holders": [
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"},
  {"name": "Presse Locale"}, {"name": "Presse Locale"}]}]}

### 5.2 W2 / screen 2: the fan event -> zones show "Plein tarif" only; from_price_mad 30000; no INVITE category
GET {{base}}/fan/events/{{match}}

### ---------- (6) Revoke ----------

### 6.1 ADMIN: revoke Karim's paper accreditation -> 200 REFUNDED, refund null; the place goes back to "Presse"
POST {{base}}/org/tickets/{{karimTicket}}/refund
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Accréditation annulée"}

### 6.2 B12 "Remboursements à faire" -> no line for this match (the next manifest delta makes the slip ANNULÉ)
GET {{base}}/org/refunds?event_id={{match}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 6.3 B3: /sales -> paid 13 (methods FREE 13), refunded 1, refunded_mad 0. Then (7): run check.sql (header): no rows.
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
